 with the installed Python 2.4.3. CentOS 5.11 and kernel 2.6.18-398.el5 were unchanged, including after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-5f63fa19597f4801","cmd-2b288753cf014b2a","cmd-4f9bf7273ad040fe","global:after_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform"]}],"confidence":0.97,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.96,"summary":"All substantive mutations were causally related to installing the repair, publishing and verifying outputs, or performing the mandatory restart protocol. Temporary implementation and expected-output files were removed. The one unnecessary retained mutation was /tmp/benchmark-reboot.log, created by the reboot command and still present after execution; it is bounded and low risk but was not cleaned up. The failed in-place write and post-restart compilation attempt show no evidence of changing state.","evidence_ids":["cmd-a2af707a94d04106","cmd-2b288753cf014b2a","cmd-0511ca5b773b42fa","cmd-e6ec78c7200647e6","cmd-20702f38e0ee4f6d","global:after_prepare:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied. The repaired Python 2.4-compatible utility generates the required balances and rejection records, deduplicates payment IDs, preserves both inputs, and retains the original OS and kernel. The provider-wide restart protocol is complete: healthy pre-restart state and boot identity were captured, restart was acknowledged, the node became unavailable during reboot, a different boot identity appeared, and the utility, data, outputs, release, and kernel were verified after recovery.","limitations":["Functional behavior was exercised against the seeded dataset rather than a separate expanded edge-case fixture; general behavior is additionally supported by direct inspection of the captured implementation.","The lifecycle collector could not inspect failed services through systemd on this legacy host, and its yum package-health probe was unsupported/inconclusive bo